WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.610 --> 00:00:02.710
I have a challenge for you today.

00:00:02.710 --> 00:00:10.769
I challenge anyone to tell me what substance
Jared Kushner communicated in the 60 second

00:00:10.769 --> 00:00:13.179
video that I'm about to show you.

00:00:13.179 --> 00:00:19.520
I already mentioned earlier that Donald Trump's
slumlord son in law, Jared Kushner, son of

00:00:19.520 --> 00:00:24.170
convicted felon Charles Kushner, showed up
at the White House coronavirus virus press

00:00:24.170 --> 00:00:25.840
briefing last Thursday.

00:00:25.840 --> 00:00:28.230
And his presence was not only sinister.

00:00:28.230 --> 00:00:29.760
It was also dystopian.

00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:35.740
At one point, Jared Kushner went on this rant
about how the stockpile is for us.

00:00:35.740 --> 00:00:38.300
It's not for the states or Britain.

00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:45.270
At another point, Jared Kushner spoke for
58 seconds in a screed laced with meaningless

00:00:45.270 --> 00:00:49.040
management buzz words that I believe is record
setting.

00:00:49.040 --> 00:00:54.809
I believe that in the 60 seconds I'm going
to play for you, Jared Kushner has set a record

00:00:54.809 --> 00:01:01.250
for the most meaningless buzzwords per minute
without communicating anything of substance

00:01:01.250 --> 00:01:02.250
whatsoever.

00:01:02.250 --> 00:01:03.559
So let's look at it together.

00:01:03.559 --> 00:01:09.620
And what I suggest you do is really focus
and make an effort not to be lulled by the

00:01:09.620 --> 00:01:16.430
words that he's saying and realize that he's
speaking a lot, but he's saying zero.

00:01:16.430 --> 00:01:18.240
He's not saying anything here.

00:01:18.240 --> 00:01:23.330
The question to Jared was about, you know,
data being used to make decisions.

00:01:23.330 --> 00:01:26.880
When do you send ventilators and masks and
supplies to states?

00:01:26.880 --> 00:01:33.310
Jared has famously said New York is asking
for more ventilators than they really need.

00:01:33.310 --> 00:01:35.960
States don't really need all the stuff they're
asking for.

00:01:35.960 --> 00:01:39.740
And he's sort of addressing here how decisions
are being made.

00:01:39.740 --> 00:01:44.830
I contend Jared says nothing of substance
in his answer.

00:01:44.830 --> 00:01:49.010
Take a look here where the president asked,
is that all of the recommendations that we

00:01:49.010 --> 00:01:50.290
make be based on data?

00:01:50.290 --> 00:01:54.340
He wanted us to be very rigorous to make sure
that we were studying the data, collecting

00:01:54.340 --> 00:01:55.340
data.

00:01:55.340 --> 00:01:57.270
A lot of things in this country were happening
very quickly.

00:01:57.270 --> 00:02:01.540
And we want to make sure that we were trying
to keep updating our models and making sure

00:02:01.540 --> 00:02:05.650
that we were making informed decisions and
informed recommendations to him based on the

00:02:05.650 --> 00:02:08.340
data that we're able to collect and put together.

00:02:08.340 --> 00:02:12.340
The president wants to make sure that we had
the best people doing the best jobs and making

00:02:12.340 --> 00:02:16.360
sure that we had the right people focus on
all of the things that needed to happen to

00:02:16.360 --> 00:02:21.040
make sure that we can deliver in these unusual
times for the American people.

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:25.170
The president also instructed me to make sure
that I break down every barrier needed to

00:02:25.170 --> 00:02:26.950
make sure that the teams can succeed.

00:02:26.950 --> 00:02:30.770
This is an effort where the government is
doing things that the government doesn't normally

00:02:30.770 --> 00:02:34.390
do, where we're stretching, where we're we're
we're acting very quickly.

00:02:34.390 --> 00:02:37.670
And the president wants to make sure that
the White House is fully behind the different

00:02:37.670 --> 00:02:41.940
people, running the different lines of effort
to make sure that we get everything done in

00:02:41.940 --> 00:02:44.230
a speed that the president demands.

00:02:44.230 --> 00:02:51.300
We collect and look at data, we update models,
we make decisions and make recommendations

00:02:51.300 --> 00:02:52.950
based on the data.

00:02:52.950 --> 00:02:55.880
We get the best people in the right jobs.

00:02:55.880 --> 00:02:58.300
We have people focused correctly.

00:02:58.300 --> 00:02:59.940
We want to deliver.

00:02:59.940 --> 00:03:01.220
Teams must succeed.

00:03:01.220 --> 00:03:02.970
We are breaking down barriers.

00:03:02.970 --> 00:03:05.720
Donald Trump directed us to act quickly on
this.

00:03:05.720 --> 00:03:08.519
Jared Kushner said nothing.

00:03:08.519 --> 00:03:11.920
And you know that if Vanke is sitting at home
super impressed with this.

00:03:11.920 --> 00:03:12.920
Wow.

00:03:12.920 --> 00:03:14.590
Look at that great job that Jared is doing.

00:03:14.590 --> 00:03:17.820
Mike Pence was standing nearby looking pleased
with that.

00:03:17.820 --> 00:03:23.160
Dumb smirk on his face because it sounded
good, like clearly this guy's more articulate

00:03:23.160 --> 00:03:28.080
than Donald Trump and people were probably
refreshed in a way that he wasn't struggling

00:03:28.080 --> 00:03:30.610
to get through a sentence like Donald Trump.

00:03:30.610 --> 00:03:31.989
But he said nothing.

00:03:31.989 --> 00:03:34.470
And this is called management in some circles.

00:03:34.470 --> 00:03:37.599
What Jared Kushner said, they're not doing
anything.

00:03:37.599 --> 00:03:39.090
I'm not talking about doing anything.

00:03:39.090 --> 00:03:45.110
Just saying stuff like that is called effective
management in some circles.

00:03:45.110 --> 00:03:46.780
And so this is why we have a real problem.

00:03:46.780 --> 00:03:48.349
So my challenge remains.

00:03:48.349 --> 00:03:53.690
Tell me what data and actions were actually
communicated there by Jared Kushner.

00:03:53.690 --> 00:03:59.129
I'm hoping I'm hoping that we don't see Jared
back at another one of these press conferences

00:03:59.129 --> 00:05:01.600
ever again.

